codex
The native-swap approach is not sufficient for first-class Windows: Windows explicitly rejects replacement when the destination is an existing directory. I’m correcting the design instead of hiding that gap—repairs will publish a new immutable generation and atomically switch a small pointer under the cross-process lock, while retaining the immediately retired generation so existing readers never lose their path. The normal cold-cache path remains unchanged.
